--- !u!114 &72715993
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 72715992}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 7cb88c33ac7b12447b79c6fd74f0c647, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::JournalManager
  journalPanel: {fileID: 0}
  journalEntriesText: {fileID: 0}
  closeButton: {fileID: 0}
  entryList: {fileID: 0}
  entryButtonPrefab: {fileID: 8510403111830143084, guid: 5f4b0cffd74292b43af0a0cb6a51660a, type: 3}
  noteScrollRect: {fileID: 0}
  discoveryNotificationText: {fileID: 0}
  notificationDuration: 3
  connectButton: {fileID: 0}
  connectionStatusText: {fileID: 0}
  selectionSlot1Text: {fileID: 0}
  selectionSlot2Text: {fileID: 0}
  clearSelectionButton: {fileID: 0}
  selectedEntryColor: {r: 0.39, g: 0.47, b: 0.52, a: 1}
  hypothesisDefinitions:
  - hypothesisID: unresolved_waterworks_work
    informationEntryID: hypothesis_unresolved_waterworks_work
    title: Unresolved Waterworks Work
    description: The anonymous package contains two incomplete records concerning the waterworks. Bell Municipal Services appears connected to the paperwork, but the purpose of the work remains unclear.
    requiredInformationID1: maintenance_record_copy
    requiredInformationID2: work_order_fragment
  - hypothesisID: unverified_departure
    informationEntryID: hypothesis_unverified_departure
    title: An Unverified Departure
    description: Evelyn accepted the departure explanation without witnessing it, and the Gazette's follow-up cited no witness to Daniel leaving. The published account appears to lack independent confirmation.
    requiredInformationID1: evelyn_accepted_account
    requiredInformationID2: gazette_followup_report
  - hypothesisID: unresolved_pump_return
    informationEntryID: hypothesis_unresolved_pump_return
    title: Unresolved Pump Return
    description: Caleb's log lacks a pump return entry. A possibly related Bell pump remains in his workshop.
    requiredInformationID1: caleb_equipment_log
    requiredInformationID2: caleb_stored_equipment
  - hypothesisID: unverified_lower_access_maintenance
    informationEntryID: hypothesis_unverified_lower_access_maintenance
    title: Unverified Lower Access Maintenance
    description: WW-91-184 is marked at the lower access, but the municipal ledger does not confirm completion.
    requiredInformationID1: municipal_status_ledger
    requiredInformationID2: waterworks_inspection_marks
  - hypothesisID: unexplained_service_barrier
    informationEntryID: hypothesis_unexplained_service_barrier
    title: Unexplained Service Barrier
    description: 'The sealed service barrier shows signs of previous adjustment or removal, but the available maintenance records do not identify it or explain its installation. The physical condition of the barrier and the documentary gap leave its history unresolved. Further records or testimony may clarify when and why the passage was closed.

'
    requiredInformationID1: waterworks_barrier_fasteners
    requiredInformationID2: waterworks_barrier_record_gap
  - hypothesisID: changed_service_access
    informationEntryID: hypothesis_changed_service_access
    title: Changed Service Access
    description: Caleb remembers a gate where a solid barrier now blocks the lower passage.
    requiredInformationID1: waterworks_service_barrier
    requiredInformationID2: caleb_barrier_recollection
  - hypothesisID: unverified_access_alteration
    informationEntryID: hypothesis_unverified_access_alteration
    title: Unverified Access Alteration
    description: The alteration register may document the changed access, but its authorization and completion are unclear.
    requiredInformationID1: municipal_facilities_alteration_register
    requiredInformationID2: caleb_barrier_recollection
  - hypothesisID: unresolved_barrier_responsibility
    informationEntryID: hypothesis_unresolved_barrier_responsibility
    title: Unresolved Barrier Responsibility
    description: Bell Municipal Services dispatched workers and equipment to the lower waterworks access in October 1991. Frank Bell acknowledges the assignment but maintains that the available records do not establish who altered the service barrier. The dispatch sheet confirms Bell's involvement in maintenance at the site, but neither it nor Frank's statement identifies who installed or modified the barrier. Responsibility remains unresolved.
    requiredInformationID1: bell_dispatch_sheet
    requiredInformationID2: frank_barrier_responsibility
  - hypothesisID: unconfirmed_oct17_visit
    informationEntryID: hypothesis_unconfirmed_oct17_visit
    title: Unconfirmed October 17 Visit
    description: Bell's log lists an October 17 site check, but he will not confirm attending that day.
    requiredInformationID1: bell_supplementary_access_log
    requiredInformationID2: frank_oct17_site_visit
  - hypothesisID: frank_lower_access_familiarity
    informationEntryID: hypothesis_frank_lower_access_familiarity
    title: Frank's Knowledge of Lower Access
    description: Frank Bell referred to the waterworks' lower service entrance without being questioned about that part of the facility. The entrance is obstructed by a service barrier whose installation and authorization remain inadequately documented. Frank's familiarity with the area may be explained by his contracting work, but his unsolicited dismissal of its significance warrants further investigation.
    requiredInformationID1: waterworks_service_barrier
    requiredInformationID2: frank_lower_access_knowledge
  - hypothesisID: unexplained_access_obstruction
    informationEntryID: hypothesis_unexplained_access_obstruction
    title: Unexplained Access Obstruction
    description: The municipal facilities alteration register records a change to the lower service access, but its authorization, installation details, and completion status remain unresolved. Physical inspection reveals that the newer barrier obstructs an older doorway whose frame and hardware appear intact. The two findings suggest that the original access arrangement was deliberately blocked, although the purpose, timing, and responsible parties have not been established.
    requiredInformationID1: municipal_facilities_alteration_register
    requiredInformationID2: waterworks_original_access_mechanism
  - hypothesisID: sealed_inspection_chamber
    informationEntryID: hypothesis_sealed_inspection_chamber
    title: The Sealed Inspection Chamber
    description: The barrier blocks the original entrance to Inspection Chamber L-02.
    requiredInformationID1: municipal_waterworks_archived_floor_plan
    requiredInformationID2: waterworks_original_access_mechanism
  - hypothesisID: possible_oct17_attendance
    informationEntryID: hypothesis_possible_oct17_attendance
    title: Possible October 17 Attendance
    description: A gatekeeper's entry places someone recorded as F. Bell at the waterworks at 6:40 PM on October 17.
    requiredInformationID1: hypothesis_unconfirmed_oct17_visit
    requiredInformationID2: waterworks_gatekeeper_register
  - hypothesisID: possible_secondary_chamber_access
    informationEntryID: hypothesis_possible_secondary_chamber_access
    title: Possible Secondary Chamber Access
    description: An opening near the auxiliary pump may provide another route into L-02.
    requiredInformationID1: hypothesis_sealed_inspection_chamber
    requiredInformationID2: waterworks_auxiliary_pump_connection
  - hypothesisID: possible_chamber_activity
    informationEntryID: hypothesis_possible_chamber_activity
    title: Possible Activity in Chamber L-02
    description: The disturbed floor and partially emptied maintenance cabinet suggest that Chamber L-02 may have been accessed or used after its original construction. Neither observation establishes when this occurred or whether it was connected to Daniel Mercer's disappearance.
    requiredInformationID1: chamber_disturbed_floor
    requiredInformationID2: chamber_maintenance_cabinet
  - hypothesisID: unexplained_chamber_disturbance
    informationEntryID: hypothesis_unexplained_chamber_disturbance
    title: Unexplained Disturbance in L-02
    description: The fabric trapped beneath the drainage grate and the marks on the pump maintenance cover suggest that the chamber contains physical traces of activity whose origin and timing have not been established. These observations warrant further investigation but do not yet identify who entered the chamber or why.
    requiredInformationID1: chamber_trapped_fabric
    requiredInformationID2: chamber_pump_cover_marks
  - hypothesisID: oct17_lower_service_access
    informationEntryID: hypothesis_oct17_lower_service_access
    title: October 17 Lower Service Access
    description: An October 17 access request coincides with Bell's recorded arrival at the waterworks.
    requiredInformationID1: chamber_concealed_access_note
    requiredInformationID2: waterworks_gatekeeper_register
  - hypothesisID: possible_daniel_metal_tag
    informationEntryID: hypothesis_possible_daniel_metal_tag
    title: Possible Connection to Daniel's Investigation
    description: The object in L-02 may resemble the numbered tag Evelyn remembers Daniel carrying.
    requiredInformationID1: chamber_recess_personal_effect
    requiredInformationID2: evelyn_daniel_metal_tag
  - hypothesisID: metal_tag_record_connection
    informationEntryID: hypothesis_metal_tag_record_connection
    title: Possible Waterworks Record Connection
    description: The object's partial marking, 184, may relate to work order WW-91-184.
    requiredInformationID1: chamber_metal_tag_marking
    requiredInformationID2: municipal_facilities_alteration_register
  - hypothesisID: deliberate_chamber_concealment
    informationEntryID: hypothesis_deliberate_chamber_concealment
    title: Possible Deliberate Concealment
    description: Daniel's remains were found behind an altered access barrier, suggesting possible deliberate concealment.
    requiredInformationID1: waterworks_preliminary_examination_report
    requiredInformationID2: hypothesis_unverified_access_alteration
  - hypothesisID: original_investigation_gap
    informationEntryID: hypothesis_original_investigation_gap
    title: Gap in the Original Investigation
    description: The original missing-person investigation did not locate Daniel's remains at the waterworks.
    requiredInformationID1: daniel_original_police_report
    requiredInformationID2: waterworks_preliminary_examination_report
  - hypothesisID: dwyer_unrecorded_waterworks_lead
    informationEntryID: hypothesis_dwyer_unrecorded_waterworks_lead
    title: Possible Unrecorded Waterworks Lead
    description: Evelyn recalls telling Dwyer about Daniel's waterworks concerns, but the surviving report omits them.
    requiredInformationID1: daniel_original_police_report
    requiredInformationID2: evelyn_dwyer_investigation_recollection
  - hypothesisID: bell_dwyer_oct17_overlap
    informationEntryID: hypothesis_bell_dwyer_oct17_overlap
    title: Bell and Dwyer at the Waterworks
    description: Bell was recorded arriving at 6:40 PM; Dwyer was dispatched to the waterworks at 7:05 PM.
    requiredInformationID1: waterworks_gatekeeper_register
    requiredInformationID2: dwyer_oct17_activity_log
  - hypothesisID: dwyer_lower_access_dispatch
    informationEntryID: hypothesis_dwyer_lower_access_dispatch
    title: Dwyer's Lower-Access Dispatch
    description: Dwyer's October 17 dispatch specifically concerned the lower service area.
    requiredInformationID1: dwyer_oct17_activity_log
    requiredInformationID2: dwyer_oct17_dispatch_slip
  - hypothesisID: dwyer_lower_access_guidance
    informationEntryID: hypothesis_dwyer_lower_access_guidance
    title: Dwyer's Route to the Lower Service Area
    description: The October 17 dispatch communications slip records a request for Deputy Michael Dwyer to attend the waterworks lower service area. Caleb Turner explains that the passage was reached through maintenance routes unfamiliar to most visitors. If Dwyer attempted to reach the specified location, he may have needed directions from someone familiar with the facility. The evidence does not establish that he entered the passage or identify anyone who assisted him.
    requiredInformationID1: dwyer_oct17_dispatch_slip
    requiredInformationID2: caleb_lower_access_directions
  - hypothesisID: possible_police_presence_in_chamber
    informationEntryID: hypothesis_possible_police_presence_in_chamber
    title: Possible Police Presence in Chamber L-02
    description: A corroded equipment tag bearing the letters GSD was discovered beside the drainage channel in Chamber L-02. An October 17, 1991 dispatch slip records Deputy Michael Dwyer being sent to the waterworks lower service area. The tag may indicate sheriff's department equipment was present in the chamber, but its age, original owner, and connection to Dwyer's visit remain unverified.
    requiredInformationID1: chamber_equipment_tag_marking
    requiredInformationID2: dwyer_oct17_dispatch_slip
  - hypothesisID: dwyer_missing_equipment_connection
    informationEntryID: hypothesis_dwyer_missing_equipment_connection
    title: Dwyer's Missing Equipment
    description: A GSD-marked tag in L-02 may belong to the inspection lamp assigned to Dwyer.
    requiredInformationID1: chamber_equipment_tag_marking
    requiredInformationID2: dwyer_equipment_assignment_register
  - hypothesisID: concealed_barrier_purpose
    informationEntryID: hypothesis_concealed_barrier_purpose
    title: The Barrier's Concealed Purpose
    description: Bell's original order omitted chamber inspection, while the municipal register concealed that restriction.
    requiredInformationID1: bell_original_barrier_work_order
    requiredInformationID2: municipal_facilities_alteration_register
  - hypothesisID: daniel_possible_platform_fall
    informationEntryID: hypothesis_daniel_possible_platform_fall
    title: Daniel's Possible Fall
    description: Daniel's injuries are consistent with a fall from the damaged maintenance platform.
    requiredInformationID1: daniel_skeletal_trauma_assessment
    requiredInformationID2: chamber_damaged_platform_railing
  - hypothesisID: billed_work_unverified
    informationEntryID: hypothesis_billed_work_unverified
    title: Unverified Billed Work
    description: Bell billed the town for WW-91-184, but the municipal ledger does not confirm the work was completed.
    requiredInformationID1: municipal_status_ledger
    requiredInformationID2: bell_billing_copy
